This is an independent, clean-room implementation. No third-party source code
was copied into this repository.

Prior art and references (concepts only, not code):
  * CVE-2026-111497 — Node.js / Brotli security advisory and upstream
    google/brotli fix.
  * The behavioral "does it decode Brotli request bodies" detection idea
    (valid Brotli body vs. an unknown Content-Encoding) is a public technique
    used by several checkers; this project reimplements it from first
    principles.

The vulnerable/patched Docker lab is built on the official `node` images,
which carry their own licenses.
